Victories change the world: Major victories change the world rather than restore the initial situation. Some confli", "truncated": true, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "agent_proposed", "book": 24, "cites": ["d1"], "element_id": "agent-lineages", "epistemic_status": "asserted", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E4", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "4e9cc396b7d08141288cabded6bbdb0cb0a99ba6ff83c1a190abdeb3d294fb46", "text": "Ysa Trant and the maintenance lineages: the Right is conditional on training, so they need the condition demonstrated or the Right is exposed. They guard craft standards and fear dilution by untrained gift-hands. Their stake in the review is an agent inference.", "truncated": false, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "agent_proposed", "book": 24, "cites": ["d2"], "element_id": "agent-mill-compact", "epistemic_status": "asserted", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E5", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "a322f67d32dc511962b079dd402274d62647a6332783378003ec3951bd05e8fc", "text": "Oona Brisk and the Mill Compact (named in the source; see unk-character-sourcing) offer hired lowland labour if it is credited against the Compact's draw. The offer is neither accepted nor refused, because the Compact's settlement is author-reserved.", "truncated": false, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "agent_proposed", "book": 24, "cites": ["d2"], "element_id": "alt-early-compact", "epistemic_status": "hypothetical", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E6", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "1a2f356d46f815e1051985e5a312f8567482740577431131a0d86d9a9efdd0c7", "text": "Oona's bid brought forward. It would displace Books 27 to 29 and press on the author-reserved settlement.", "truncated": false, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "unknown_legacy", "book": 24, "cites": ["d1"], "element_id": "cons-belief-plural", "epistemic_status": "unknown_legacy", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E7", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "1500f7b4ee3999f57270c844027cd2fd4dbc5b77aac3a4e8b8c7ed5c4db89dbf", "text": "The cohort's belief is no longer uniform. The Brightwater inheritance splits into counted and uncounted practice within one generation, so plurality of practice now crosses generations as well as communities.", "truncated": false, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "agent_proposed", "book": 24, "cites": ["d1"], "element_id": "fn-question", "epistemic_status": "asserted", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E8", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "8854e7775cafa42e7065586594712d8a9c14eab42c5ce02b28d00a34079a8ca1", "text": "Book 24 is where the Long Return's labour gap is first met by people rather than by a schedule. A generation that refuses to be counted is asked to give back the water before it is owed. The Book exercises the Old Hand, the Ledger and the Source, and exports one new kind of record: a public capability record, separate from debt, tally and aggregate balance, that says who can repair rather than who", "truncated": true, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "derived", "book": 24, "cites": ["d1"], "element_id": "inh-cohort-belief", "epistemic_status": "asserted", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E9", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "cb01b7bc79bce1b851ced6c37fed43162fd03e71c28871391c40bb9455801204", "text": "A generation that came of age after Book 20 has never seen the labour, because lineage crews perform it under the Right.", "truncated": false, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "agent_proposed", "book": 24, "cites": ["d1"], "element_id": "inh-right-condition", "epistemic_status": "asserted", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E10", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "92167788e69b2896933bbfb0d779234d04b16e51f685323e102b67a41d6bb81b", "text": "The Special Draw Right is conditional on training apprentices from outside the lineage. Its review point falls in Book 24 (agent-proposed as P1; the source gives a reversal for it).", "truncated": false, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "derived", "book": 24, "cites": ["d1"], "element_id": "later-cohort-seat", "epistemic_status": "hypothetical", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E11", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "4fdad0ce477d0370c085d7898b25b55dc8527285881a3cf730b5b4b4c06fde7d", "text": "The cohort, now practising both counted and uncounted return, may claim standing in how the valley coordinates its channel work. Book 24 names no body that would grant that standing and creates none.", "truncated": false, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "unknown_legacy", "book": 24, "cites": ["d2"], "element_id": "later-oona-offer", "epistemic_status": "unknown_legacy", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E12", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "41e80f6b333e6c61797ea97bbfa5db4794b282e7a1928ba58bea341fbc1dc98a", "text": "Oona's standing offer meets a valley with some hands of its own before the Book 27 to 29 bid.", "truncated": false, "version_sha256": null}, {"attribution": "unknown_legacy", "book": 24, "cites": ["d2"], "element_id": "res-custody-declined", "epistemic_status": "unknown_legacy", "freshness": "current_read", "id": "E13", "kind": "book_element", "owner": "Working Book owner, read now", "source": "working_book", "source_sha256": "d778e0d4f20f5496f5acb025ff9db95736103e1514a1f234acddc85d0bbba6f6", "text": "The remnant's cus